  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1118 PM CDT Sun Apr 19 2026\n\nSurface high pressure will slide into the area beginning late \nMonday. Warmer air will begin to filter in starting on Tuesday, with \nthe passage of a warm front that will also bring a brief period of \nclouds. As the new air mass makes itself at home, highs will rise by \nmid-week into the low 80s under clear skies. As for rain chances, \nthe end of the week looks active, but not too many details on that \nright now in the guidance. QPF amounts currently look promising, but \nbeing that rain is 6 days out temporally, we will have to wait and \nsee before we start advertising amounts. Stay tuned!",
